# ymsdk

Go client for the Yandex Messenger Bot API, covering all 28 documented
endpoints. The full reference is
[`skills/ymsdk/references/reference.md`](../../skills/ymsdk/references/reference.md);
complete working programs are in
[`recipes.md`](../../skills/ymsdk/references/recipes.md). Read the reference
before writing anything beyond a one-line change.

## The traps

These compile and look correct, and fail in production.

- **Retries are off by default** — `RetryStrategy.MaxAttempts` is 1. Set it to 3.
- **Never set `DisableAutoPayloadID`** without supplying your own key. The
  generated `payload_id` stops a retried send from posting twice on `sendText`,
  `sendSticker`, `sendSystemMessage` and `createPoll`; uploads and the `share*`
  resends accept no such key, so retrying one of those can duplicate.
- **Guard `u.Chat`, `u.From` and attachment fields** — reaction events,
  membership changes and button presses are updates with no text and no chat.
- **`Update.Images` is `[][]ym.Image`** — outer slice per image, inner slice per
  size variant. Call `u.OriginalImages()`; do not flatten by hand.
- **An incoming file is `u.Document`**, not `u.File`.
- **Webhook handlers have a 1-second budget** — use `updates.NewWebhookHandler`
  and never call the API on the request path. Delivery is at-least-once.
- **`getUpdates` permanently erases updates below the offset.** Advance only
  after handling them.
- **Use `updates.Run`, not `PollLoop`** — the latter is deprecated and stops on
  the first error.
- **Escape echoed user text** with `ym.EscapeMarkdown`, or wrap it in `ym.Code`.

## Conventions

- Address recipients with `ym.Target` — `ChatTarget`, `LoginTarget`,
  `UserIDTarget` — exactly one field set.
- Match errors with `errors.Is` on the `ymerrors` sentinels and `errors.As` for
  `*ymerrors.APIError` (`HTTPStatus`, `Description`, `RequestID`, `RetryAfter`).
- Use the `ym.Endpoint*` constants, never a path literal.
- Reaction and membership events require `get_reactions` / `get_members_changed`
  to be switched on via `cs.Self.Update`.
